# Copy to .cursorignore (leading dot) in your repo root.
#
# Agents usually can't write this file themselves — it controls their own
# access, so Cursor keeps it in human hands. That's also why it works: unlike a
# written instruction in AGENTS.md, this is enforced by the tool rather than
# requested of the model. Rules ask nicely; this blocks access.
#
# Limit worth knowing: Cursor's docs say terminal and MCP tools cannot block
# access to ignored files, so `cat .ctx/scratchpad.md` still works. This raises
# the cost of an accident. It is not a security boundary.

.ctx/scratchpad.md

# Add anything else that's human-only or sensitive, e.g.
# .env
# .env.*
# secrets/
# *.pem
